      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Semiconductor quantum dots provided a practical solid-state source of single and indistinguishable photons, advancing quantum optics and photonic quantum information.",
        "attribution": "The proposed names represent influential demonstrations and development of quantum-dot single-photon sources, but the advance involved rapid contributions from several experimental groups.",
        "maturity": "Single-photon emission is robust, and indistinguishable photons have been demonstrated; source efficiency, indistinguishability, and integration have improved substantially.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The long-term impact relative to other single-photon platforms remains uncertain.",
